SCALE — the world/swarm run at this fraction of speed when bullet-time engages. Source: src/core/Game.ts:417 slowMotionTarget = 0.25.", "name" => "slowMoScale", "title" => "Slow-mo scale (bullet-time)", "type" => "string", "validation" => %{"pattern" => "^-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?$"}}], false, "document", [], "production", [], "history", [], "private", [], [], %{"channels" => [%{"name" => "real_dt", "note" => "Raw clamped wall-clock delta. Camera, UI, and the slow-mo ease itself consume this — they must NOT slow down when gameplay does. _clamped is also accumulated into elapsed_real_seconds() as the deterministic monotonic stopwatch.", "scaledBy" => "none — raw clamped wall-clock delta (minf(real_delta, MAX_DELTA))"}, %{"name" => "player_dt", "note" => "Player-simulation delta: real time scaled by the eased slow-motion factor and the death crawl (1% speed via DEATH_SLOW_SCALE when is_dead). The player's own update runs on this so it reacts to bullet-time but stays decoupled from the world speed-up.", "scaledBy" => "real_dt * slow_motion_scale * (0.01 if is_dead else 1.0)"}, %{"name" => "physics_dt", "note" => "World / physics delta: player_dt times the flat game_speed speed-up. The world, projectiles, and collision integration step on this.", "scaledBy" => "player_dt * game_speed (1.2)"}, %{"name" => "enemy_dt", "note" => "Enemy-swarm delta: identical to physics_dt except hard-gated to 0.0 when enemies_frozen — the swarm halts in place while every other channel keeps advancing. This is exactly what Engine.time_scale cannot express.", "scaledBy" => "physics_dt, hard-gated to 0.0 when enemies_frozen"}], "gameSpeed" => "1.2", "slowMoScale" => "0.25", "title" => "GameClock"}, [], %{}, %{}, false, %{}, ~U[2026-10-13 18:36:41.488427Z], ~U[2026-10-13 18:36:41.488427Z], "ca3f23ad-d82e-4ec8-ab4b-6bdc27795fe6"]
